※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4505

※ What `⎕typeof` answers is a type, and a type is not a value: there is
※ nothing for one to be at run time, which is why the representation is
※ deliberately unspecified.  Where it may stand is the one place the answer is
※ wanted and never has to exist.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let n: u8 = 5u8
    if ⎕typeof(n) = u8:
        1u8
    else:
        0u8
